// Reassigning an immutable binding is a **compile-time** error (E0006), not a runtime one — so it is
// caught even on a branch that never executes. Here the write is inside `if false { … }`, which the
// program never reaches, yet the reassignment is still rejected statically. The write is on line 9,
// column 3.
// expect: error E0006 at 9:3
// expect: exit 1
x = 1;
if false {
  x = 2;
}
echo x;
